<main>
  <h1>local_LLM</h1>
  <p class="lede">A self-hosted, GPU-accelerated local LLM stack — llama.cpp inference, a chat UI, anonymous search, and a portal to tie it together. Runs on a single Docker host, fronted by Caddy.</p>

  <div class="card-links">
    <a href="api.html">
      <div class="card-title">API</div>
      <div class="card-desc">Endpoint, curl example, OpenCode/VSCode setup, CA certificate install</div>
    </a>
    <a href="environment.html">
      <div class="card-title">Environment</div>
      <div class="card-desc">Architecture diagram — Caddy routing, the LLM stack, the optional Obs stack</div>
    </a>
    <a href="hardware.html">
      <div class="card-title">Hardware</div>
      <div class="card-desc">GPU/CPU/RAM this deployment is actually running on</div>
    </a>
  </div>

  <h2>What's running</h2>
  <p>Dashy (portal), OpenWebUI (chat), SearXNG (anonymous search), and <code>llm-server</code> (llama.cpp's OpenAI-compatible API) — all reverse-proxied through Caddy, the sole entry point. An optional monitoring stack (Prometheus + Grafana + exporters) can run alongside. See <a href="environment.html">Environment</a> for how it all fits together.</p>
</main>

